Hi folks,

Richard Ishida (chair of W3C Internationalization GEO project)
just asked a question about what fonts are usually installed
on various operating system platforms (Windows/XP, Linux, etc.)
and therefore available for use in HTML documents (on the
W3C Internationalization mailing list).  

The best response so far is to look at Markus Kuhn's info at:

http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mgk25/unicode.html#fonts

This discussion will probably be highly relevant for the PWG's
Character Repertoires WG and for FSG's Driver and Renderer WG.

